WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:02.080
Next question, David.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:06.050
I see that Joe Biden is doing really well
in the polls.

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:10.640
What is the point of no return for Donald
Trump's polling?

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.400
So let me first give you.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.700
For practical purposes.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.700
Answer.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:16.700
Imagine.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:17.820
There is no point of no return.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:19.689
Even if Trump is losing by 20.

00:00:19.689 --> 00:00:24.419
On November 2nd, you go out and you vote on
November 3rd because you just don't know what's

00:00:24.419 --> 00:00:25.689
going to happen in your state.

00:00:25.689 --> 00:00:28.909
We all have to vote, et cetera.

00:00:28.909 --> 00:00:29.909
Now.

00:00:29.909 --> 00:00:36.070
I believe that if on October 1st, about a
month before the election, the numbers are

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:38.020
what they are today.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.460
I believe it's it's over for Donald Trump.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.120
Short of a true miracle.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.370
We're not talking.

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.680
Think back to 2016.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.440
2016, heading into election, into the election
day.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.060
The national polling was Hillary is up by
three point two.

00:00:53.060 --> 00:01:00.090
And Hillary won by two point one in the national
popular vote, of course, because of 77000

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.090
votes in three states.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:02.829
Electorally, she ultimately lost.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:08.530
We're talking about, you know, an eight to
nine point lead for Joe Biden right now.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:14.580
And if those are the numbers going into the
election, Joe Biden is is going to win.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.609
Now, what could change this?

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:21.880
Listen, if Joe Biden's indicted between now
and November, if Joe Biden dies between now

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:27.509
and November, if Trump personally cures cancer
on Halloween, writes it.

00:01:27.509 --> 00:01:31.929
These are the types of things where if on
October 1st, Biden's up eight and a half.

00:01:31.929 --> 00:01:35.070
That's what you need to turn it around.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:38.812
William Barr and Mitch McConnell could try
to pull something underhanded, you know, maybe

00:01:38.812 --> 00:01:42.639
some kind of B.S. investigation into Joe or
Hunter Biden.

00:01:42.639 --> 00:01:43.670
Maybe it would have an impact.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.200
Honestly, at this point, I don't even know
that that would make a difference.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.899
A lot of people would not take it seriously.

00:01:48.899 --> 00:01:52.799
You know, Trump's retweeting Chuck Woolery
while attacking Anthony Foushee on the issue

00:01:52.799 --> 00:01:54.100
of Corona virus.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:58.749
It's clear that Trump has lost credibility
with a large swath of the American electorate

00:01:58.749 --> 00:02:02.479
each day that Trump doesn't take the lead
in the polling.

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:04.670
It's a day he loses to turn it around.

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:11.009
And, you know, I've been getting e-mails about
should Joe Biden even bother to debate Trump?

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:13.270
The idea now being.

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:17.120
Trump's doing so much self-inflicted damage.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.540
Why would Joe Biden even come out and debate?

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:23.960
Now, of course, your view on that depends
on how well you think Joe Biden would do.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:25.070
I hope they debate.

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:29.460
I look forward to watching the debates, but
I do think there's a question there.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.430
Like, is it easy to just let Trump continue
to self-destruct?

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:34.450
Maybe debating him doesn't even really make
sense.

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:39.120
Although, again, if Trump is willing and Biden
is not, it would look bad for Joe Biden.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:43.650
The other difference, I think that's important
in terms of looking at the polling in 2016

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:50.210
and looking at the polling today, is that
in 2016, Donald Trump was running on being

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:52.800
the anti Washington, D.C. guy.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:59.770
He was riding a wave of and tie establishment
sentiment, which may have helped him as Hillary

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:05.239
Clinton was dogged by the James Comey press
conference, et cetera.

00:03:05.239 --> 00:03:07.060
Trump is the establishment right now.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.590
So that is not going to work.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:14.680
And in terms of looking at why Trump isn't
doing well in the polls, the leading drag

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:22.180
factors for Trump are corona virus handling
economy, racial issues as connected to the

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.590
George Floyd protests.

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:26.700
Could those changed between now and November?

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:27.700
Yeah, theoretically.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:31.340
I mean, Corona virus could be gotten more
under control right now.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:33.530
It says out of control, as it's been.

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:37.040
If that were to happen, the economy could
start to turn around.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:38.480
Three and a half months is not that long.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:42.010
And we've already been in corona virus mode
for about five months.

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:44.000
So how likely that is is a question mark.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:49.710
But I would see the potent point of no return
as sometime around October 1st, barring something

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:53.870
earth shattering, earth shattering, like an
indictment of Joe Biden.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:04:00.189
Or again, as I said, Trump personally cures
cancer or develops a corona virus vaccine.

